Antipodal summand pairs and multiplicative unit visibility (S571)
==============================================================================
Odd C=2n-1 nodes: summand pairs {a,C-a} are exactly antipodal residue pairs.
Units modulo C are the multiplicative clocks that can move a missed pair to {+1,-1}.
Even C nodes have a fixed midpoint C/2, the missing distinct-summand/apex pair.

